+## On-demand HTTP sessions
+
+For a scale-to-zero Streamable HTTP server, opt in with:
+
+```yaml
+mcp_servers:
+  browser:
+    url: https://mcp.example.com/mcp
+    on_demand: true
+    idle_timeout_seconds: 10
+```
+
+Hermes discovers the catalog on startup and retains it while the session is
+closed. The separate `lazy` cache option does not apply in this mode. After idling, the
+next call opens a fresh session; Hermes does not poll to keep it alive. If
+first discovery fails before any catalog exists, reload the MCP configuration
+once the endpoint is reachable. There is no background retry loop. This mode
+supports static headers or no authentication, not interactive OAuth or SSE.
+Treat lost responses after dispatch as an unknown outcome; Hermes does not
+automatically retry those operations. A new session also does not restore
+server-side state such as open browser tabs.
+
 ## Quick start
 
 1. MCP support ships with the standard install — no extra step needed.
